DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nederlands Letterenfonds: Project Grants for Literary Tra
 nslators (August 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Project subsidies from the Nederlands Letterenfonds for advance
 d literary translators with a current publishing contract for a translatio
 n from or into Dutch. The next round closes 15 August 2026\; decisions are
  made approximately four months after the deadline (December). ELIGIBILITY
 : literary translators with a substantial published portfolio and a contra
 cted translation project\; primary income must be below EUR 52\,500.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Nederlands Letterenfonds (Dutch Foundation for Literature)\nLo
 cation: Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)\nAward: Project-based subsidy. Income cap EUR 52\,500 for 
 primary income. Standard minimum rates: EUR 0.0802/word for prose\; EUR 2.
 92/line for poetry. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, scaled 
 to the contracted translation\n\nMore: https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-car
 ibbean/funding/project-grants-for-literary-translators?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-caribbean/funding/project-grants-for-li
 terary-translators?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oif-artist-mobility-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: OIF: Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultu
 ral Goods 2026 (Francophonie)
DESCRIPTION:The OIF Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultural
  Goods programme provides grants of up to EUR 5\,000 for mobility (travel\
 , accommodation\, visa fees\, logistics) and up to EUR 2\,500 for circulat
 ion of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs) within the Fran
 cophone zone\; both can be combined. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists and
  established artistic collectives with a demonstrated connection to the Fr
 ancophone space (by nationality\, working language\, or artistic collabora
 tions)\, residing in an OIF member state\, with minimum 2 years of experie
 nce in the cultural or artistic sector\; must directly manage the project 
 (not act as intermediaries)\; one application per individual per call. ELI
 GIBLE DISCIPLINES: live performance (music\, theatre\, dance\, comedy\, st
 orytelling)\, cinema/audiovisual\, literature/publishing\, and visual arts
 . PRIORITY given to projects promoting gender equality\, women artists\, c
 reators under 35\, and South-South mobility. Projects must take place betw
 een 25 March and 30 November 2026. Multiple selection sessions throughout 
 the year\; call open until 31 August 2026. Information webinars: 11 March\
 , 13 May\, and 8 July 2026 at 3 PM Paris time. Contact: culture.dlc@franco
 phonie.org. Apply at https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicatio
 ns/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Organisation internationale de la Francophonie (OIF)\nLocation: Fra
 ncophone zone (OIF member states globally)\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 for ar
 tist mobility (travel\, accommodation\, visas\, logistics). Up to EUR 2\,5
 00 for circulation of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs).
  Both can be combined. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies or tours
  of 5 days to 3 months. Projects must take place between 25 March and 30 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicat
 ions/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applications/soutien-a-la-ci
 rculation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Francophone zone (OIF member states globally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-comic-creation-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Comic Creation Grant
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's comic creation grant supports the development of
  comic projects intended for publication\, including digital formats. Appl
 icants must have published at least one independent work with a profession
 al publisher or the equivalent in magazines. ELIGIBILITY: requires a conne
 ction to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regu
 lar artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without 
 a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: maximum CHF 25\,000. Submission deadline 1 Sep
 tember (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: P
 ro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based comic creato
 rs.\nAward: Maximum CHF 25\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Creation p
 hase for a comic project intended for publication\; deadline 1 September.\
 n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/comic-creation-grant?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/comic-creation-grant?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based comic creators.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-literary-creation-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Literary Creation Grant
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's literary creation grant supports the development
  of literary projects intended for publication\, including fiction\, child
 ren's and youth literature\, poetry\, drama\, and spoken word. Applicants 
 must have prior published work\, a premiere\, or professional performances
 . ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, o
 r permanent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not
  open to practitioners without a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: up to CHF 25\,0
 00 for writing\, CHF 18\,000 for theatre texts\, or CHF 15\,000 for perfor
 mative literary projects. Deadlines twice a year: 1 March (23:59 CET) and 
 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based authors
  and collectives.\nAward: Up to CHF 25\,000 (writing)\, CHF 18\,000 (theat
 re texts)\, or CHF 15\,000 (performative literary projects). No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Creation phase for a literary project intended for publi
 cation\; deadlines twice yearly (1 March and 1 September).\n\nMore: https:
 //prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/literary-creation-grant?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/literary-creation-grant?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based authors and collectives.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sloan-foundation-book-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alfred P. Sloan Foundation: Book Grants (Public Understan
 ding of Science and Technology)
DESCRIPTION:The one Sloan program that funds individuals directly: grants f
 or authors researching and writing nonfiction books that bring science and
  technology to a general audience. Over 200 authors supported since 1996. 
 Favoured topics include elucidating confusing or controversial scientific 
 subjects\, profiles of figures in science and technology\, science-technol
 ogy-art connections\, women and science\, and the culture and philosophy o
 f science. Start with a letter of inquiry to program director Doron Weber\
 ; full proposals are by invitation only. Reviewed three times a year: LOIs
  by 1 September (decision by 15 February)\, 1 January (by 31 May) and 1 Ma
 y (by 31 October). No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Alfred P. Sloan Fo
 undation\nLocation: Remote / anywhere (US foundation\; grants paid directl
 y to authors or via a nonprofit host)\nAward: Typically up to $60\,000 per
  book grant\nDuration: Project-based (book research and writing)\n\nMore: 
 https://sloan.org/programs/public-understanding/books?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sloan.org/programs/public-understanding/books?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / anywhere (US foundation\; grants paid directly to authors
  or via a nonprofit host)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:printed-matter-publisher-work-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Printed Matter Publisher Work Grant 2026
DESCRIPTION:Third annual cycle of Printed Matter's Publisher Work Grant\, s
 upported by Wagner Foundation. Three unrestricted grants of $10\,000 go to
  independent artists' book publishers\, acknowledging past work and provid
 ing capacity-building funds for future book projects and publisher sustain
 ability. ELIGIBILITY: independent imprints with an 'independent spirit\,' 
 generally small in scale\, with a publishing history of one or more years 
 and one or more titles per year\, currently active with future titles in t
 he works\; open to publishers based anywhere (international presses encour
 aged). NOT for individual artists seeking to publish their own work\, nor 
 for commercial presses that exclusively publish client work\; more establi
 shed\, well-funded\, or institutionally supported publishers may be deprio
 ritised. Funds are unrestricted (production\, artists' fees\, equipment\, 
 studio costs\, rent\, etc.). Applications reviewed by Printed Matter and a
  guest jury based on the imprint's body of work\, upcoming projects\, and 
 potential impact. Selected presses also receive a highlighted presence at 
 a 2026 Printed Matter Art Book Fair (travel and accommodation are the gran
 tee's responsibility). Deadline: Sunday 4 October 2026\, 11:59PM EST.\n\nO
 rganisation: Printed Matter\nLocation: New York\, USA-based\; open to publ
 ishers based anywhere in the world\nAward: Three unrestricted grants of $1
 0\,000 USD each\, plus a featured exhibitor presence (complimentary table)
  at a forthcoming Printed Matter NY or LA Art Book Fair. No application fe
 e.\nDuration: Unrestricted\, capacity-building award (no obligation to rea
 lise a particular project)\n\nMore: https://www.printedmatter.org/workgran
 t?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.printedmatter.org/workgrant?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York\, USA-based\; open to publishers based anywhere in the wo
 rld
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paul-mellon-centre-author-grants-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Paul Mellon Centre: Author Grants (Autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Paul Mellon Centre funds scholarship and dissemination in B
 ritish art\, visual culture and architectural history\, from the medieval 
 period to the present and across the relevant geographical and cultural co
 ntexts. This is the Autumn 2026 round\, the first under the Centre's restr
 uctured funding scheme announced earlier in 2026\, and all grants in the r
 ound close together on Monday 14 September 2026 at 23:59 BST. ELIGIBILITY:
  the Centre's funding is open to INTERNATIONAL applicants\, not just UK-ba
 sed ones (the exceptions are the MA/MPhil Studentship and Doctoral Scholar
 ship\, which are not part of this round). Every applicant must show how th
 e award advances their research on British art\, visual culture and/or arc
 hitecture. SUPPORT: general application guidance\, an updated FAQ and the 
 Our Funding Focus page set out what the Centre looks for\, and there are w
 riteups of previously successful projects. The grants team will take speci
 fic questions or arrange a call at grants@paul-mellon-centre.ac.uk. No app
 lication fee. THIS GRANT: up to GBP 6\,000 for INDIVIDUALS disseminating r
 esearch on British art through publication\, covering monographs\, edited 
 collections\, catalogues and articles. It funds the practical side of publ
 ishing\, image copyright fees being the example the Centre gives. This is 
 the one grant in the Autumn round aimed at individual authors rather than 
 organisations.\n\nOrganisation: Paul Mellon Centre for Studies in British 
 Art\nLocation: London-based funder. Applications open internationally\; th
 e research must concern British art\, visual culture and/or architectural 
 history.\nAward: Up to GBP 6\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Autumn 2
 026 round\; applications close Monday 14 September 2026 at 23:59 BST\n\nMo
 re: https://www.paul-mellon-centre.ac.uk/about/news/autumn-round-of-fundin
 g-opportunities-open?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
URL:https://www.paul-mellon-centre.ac.uk/about/news/autumn-round-of-funding
 -opportunities-open?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
LOCATION:London-based funder. Applications open internationally\; the resea
 rch must concern British art\, visual culture and/or architectural history
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:south-arts-literary-arts-project-grants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261008
SUMMARY:Deadline: Literary Arts Project Grants 2027
DESCRIPTION:South Arts' Literary Arts Project Grants fund up to USD 5\,000 
 for the creation and publishing of creative literary work (journals\, book
 s\, anthologies) and for community engagement projects such as reading ser
 ies\, festivals and podcasts. Eligible expenses include personnel\, artist
  fees\, editorial services\, travel\, marketing\, facility rental and insu
 rance. ELIGIBILITY: independent nonprofit literary arts organizations\, in
 dependent publishers\, and small presses including literary journals\, hea
 dquartered in the nine-state South Arts region (Alabama\, Florida\, Georgi
 a\, Kentucky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina a
 nd Tennessee) with an established literary arts mission. This is an organi
 zational grant\, not an individual one\; individual writers should look at
  the Southern Prize for Literature instead. Applications opened 12 August 
 2026\; award notifications in November 2026\, with a final report due 30 J
 une 2027\, and all expenses must occur between 1 July 2026 and 30 June 202
 7. Deadline 7 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: South Arts\nLocation: USA\, n
 ine-state South Arts region: Alabama\, Florida\, Georgia\, Kentucky\, Loui
 siana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and Tennessee.\nAwar
 d: Up to USD 5\,000 per project. Eligible expenses include personnel\, art
 ist fees\, editorial services\, travel\, marketing\, facility rental and i
 nsurance. No application fee.\nDuration: All expenses must occur between 1
  July 2026 and 30 June 2027\n\nMore: https://www.southarts.org/grants-oppo
 rtunities/literary-arts-project-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.southarts.org/grants-opportunities/literary-arts-project-gr
 ants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA\, nine-state South Arts region: Alabama\, Florida\, Georgia\, 
 Kentucky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and T
 ennessee.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:adagp-sgdl-arcane-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arcane Grant 2026 for Artist Books
DESCRIPTION:Artists' books get little support\, financially or in distribut
 ion\, despite their place in art history and in the careers of the people 
 who make them. ADAGP\, the French collecting society for copyright in the 
 visual arts\, and SGDL\, the French society of authors\, created the Arcan
 e grant in response: EUR 9\,000 to one winning project for the conception 
 and production of an artist's book made collaboratively by a visual artist
  and a writer. WHO CAN APPLY: a pair consisting of a professional visual a
 rtist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at least fi
 ve years\, or a French national living abroad) and a French-language autho
 r working in fiction\, non-fiction\, poetry\, children's literature or the
 atre who has already been published by a publisher. A trio is also possibl
 e where a publishing structure joins the project. WHAT COUNTS AS AN ARTIST
 'S BOOK: a creation\, a work of art in book form\, in a limited print run 
 of between 1 and 500 copies\, which may be signed or numbered. Explicitly 
 not eligible: magazines\, fanzines\, limited editions of an ordinary book\
 , and any publication that simply presents an artist's work\, such as mono
 graphs or illustrated books. APPLICATION: the file must be in French and i
 ncludes a jointly written project presentation of up to three pages coveri
 ng the artistic and editorial vision\, constituent elements\, methods of r
 ealisation and desired final form\; a one-page technical sheet giving titl
 e\, print run\, format\, page count\, paper quality\, printing techniques 
 and materials\; a provisional timetable\; and a detailed balanced provisio
 nal budget of expenses and financing. Artistic elements are a CV of exhibi
 tions and publications (2 pages) and a portfolio with website link (10 pag
 es) for the artist\, a CV and website link for the author (2 pages)\, and 
 a one-page editorial line for the publishing structure if there is one\; c
 ontact details must be omitted from these. Administrative elements are swo
 rn declarations that the project is a new creation with copyright held sol
 ely by the pair\, that the artist is from the French scene\, and\, if appl
 icable\, that the publishing structure undertakes to publish the work. Tem
 plates are downloadable from the Required Documents page. TIMELINE: call l
 aunched 7 July 2026\, applications close 7 September 2026 at 2pm\, jury me
 ets November 2026\, winner announced end of November 2026\, and the work m
 ust be published within two years of that announcement. The regulations mu
 st be read before applying\, and submitting an application constitutes acc
 eptance of them. Contact: arcane@adagp.fr.\n\nOrganisation: ADAGP and SGDL
  (Societe des Gens de Lettres)\nLocation: France. Open to a professional v
 isual artist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at l
 east five years\, or of French nationality living abroad) paired with a Fr
 ench-language author.\nAward: EUR 9\,000 to the single winning project\, s
 upporting the conception and production of an artist's book. NOTE ON TAX: 
 ADAGP grants count as primary artistic income under the French Intellectua
 l Property Code (art. L112-2)\, so the sum falls under the artist-author s
 ocial security and tax regime\, subject to URSSAF contributions and income
  tax declared as non-commercial profits (micro-BNC or controlled declarati
 on). VAT is not due. No application fee.\nDuration: The winning duo or tri
 o commits to publishing the artist's book within two years of the announce
 ment\n\nMore: https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=pr
 ogramme&cid=187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=programme&cid
 =187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:France. Open to a professional visual artist from the French scene
  (working or residing in France for at least five years\, or of French nat
 ionality living abroad) paired with a French-language author.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:africa-no-filter-voices-for-climate-justice-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: Africa No Filter: Voices for Climate Justice 2026
DESCRIPTION:Voices for Climate Justice supports African storytellers making
  work about how climate finance reaches the continent as debt rather than 
 as grants. The framing of the call: African nations are being pushed furth
 er into debt through loans despite the continent's minimal contribution to
  the crisis\, with many governments spending more on debt repayment than o
 n health and climate adaptation combined. WHO IT IS FOR: journalists\, con
 tent creators\, podcasters\, vloggers\, muralists and data visualizers. WH
 AT YOU GET: a 12-month programme delivered with Comic Relief giving 15 to 
 20 storytellers training in climate justice\, data storytelling and narrat
 ive framing\, then mentorship and work with researchers and partners to de
 velop accurate\, research-based stories\, plus content amplification and g
 rants of up to USD 4\,000. ELIGIBILITY: aged 18 or over\; based in one of 
 the ten listed countries\; an active and highly engaged platform (podcast\
 , YouTube channel\, TikTok\, Facebook\, Instagram\, publication or data vi
 sualization portfolio) running for more than a year\; a combined audience 
 of 5\,000 or more followers across Instagram\, TikTok\, Facebook\, Twitter
 /X and Snapchat for content creators and data visualizers\, while journali
 sts may instead demonstrate reach through publication circulation\; conten
 t creators must be unsigned and not represented by an agent\, though journ
 alists may be affiliated with a publication provided the submitted work an
 d content rights remain their own\; a commitment to publishing at least fo
 ur pieces on gender\, debt and fossil fuels over at least six months\; and
  individual applicants only\, no organisations or agencies. Proposals must
  focus on the campaign's core themes of climate justice\, gender\, debt an
 d fossil fuels in Africa. NOT CONSIDERED: incomplete applications\, postal
  or email submissions\, hacked material\, vulgar\, racist\, sexist or homo
 phobic material\, work reinforcing stereotypes of Africa as poor\, corrupt
 \, diseased\, conflict-ridden or lacking agency\, and accounts or posts bo
 osted by paid engagement. HOW TO APPLY: prepare a pitch deck of no more th
 an 5 slides or a video of no more than 60 seconds connecting gender\, debt
  and fossil fuels in Africa\, then submit through the ANF application port
 al with links to your platforms and a short description of the audience yo
 u plan to reach. Content may be delivered in English or French. Selection 
 weighs originality of the idea\, relevance to ANF's mission of storytellin
 g beyond stereotypes\, relevance to the gender-debt-fossil fuel focus\, an
 d reach or standing on your platform or in your community. Only shortliste
 d candidates are notified.\n\nOrganisation: Africa No Filter\, in partners
 hip with Comic Relief\nLocation: Applicants must be based in Mozambique\, 
 Uganda\, Nigeria\, Angola\, Chad\, the Republic of Congo\, Tanzania\, Sout
 h Sudan\, Malawi or Zambia.\nAward: Grants of up to USD 4\,000 (the call s
 tates a range of USD 0 to 4\,000)\, alongside training\, mentorship and co
 ntent amplification. Between 15 and 20 storytellers will be supported. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: 12-month programme. Applications opened 11 Aug
 ust 2026 and are reviewed on a rolling basis\; deadline 25 September 2026 
 at 18:00 GMT. Screening 5 October\, interviews 9 October\, outcomes commun
 icated in the first week of October and grantees announced 15 October 2026
 .\n\nMore: https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/community/voices-for-clim
 ate-justice/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/community/voices-for-climate-just
 ice/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must be based in Mozambique\, Uganda\, Nigeria\, Angola
 \, Chad\, the Republic of Congo\, Tanzania\, South Sudan\, Malawi or Zambi
 a.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:africa-no-filter-kekere-storytellers-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Africa No Filter: Kekere Storytellers Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Kekere Storytellers Fund pays micro-grants to emerging Afri
 can storytellers who are already creating and publishing work that offers 
 fresh and alternative perspectives on the continent\, showing an Africa th
 at is innovative\, evolving and creative rather than defined by poverty\, 
 conflict\, disease\, poor leadership and corruption. Africa No Filter desc
 ribes the fund as its way of getting funding\, which is limited and rarely
  accessed by up-and-coming storytellers\, to artists\, journalists and con
 tent creators. PREREQUISITE: applicants must first be members of Africa No
  Filter's African Narrative Collective\, so join that before applying. ELI
 GIBILITY: African\, based anywhere in Africa or the diaspora\; under 35\; 
 able to work in English or French\; a track record of ground-breaking work
  that challenges stereotypical narratives about your community\, country o
 r the continent\; at least two years of related work experience\; a minimu
 m of 5\,000 followers across Twitter\, Facebook\, TikTok\, Instagram and Y
 ouTube\; and falling into at least one of two categories\, MEDIA AND CONTE
 NT CREATORS (journalist\, blogger\, vlogger\, podcaster\, fiction and non-
 fiction writer\, photographer) or ARTISTS (poet\, musician\, spoken word p
 oet\, dancer\, painter\, sculptor\, illustrator\, animator). NOT ELIGIBLE:
  filmmakers\, who are directed to ANF's Last Mile Film Fund instead\; stor
 ytellers without evidence of narrative-shifting work\; requests to buy equ
 ipment such as cameras or laptops\; and requests to host or attend events 
 such as workshops\, festivals or conferences. WHAT ANF IS LOOKING FOR: an 
 interesting\, unique story about Africa that amplifies unheard voices\, ch
 allenges global perspectives and introduces contemporary narratives\, with
  a clear sense of what you want the reader or viewer to take away and the 
 impact you want to create locally and globally.\n\nOrganisation: Africa No
  Filter\nLocation: Africans based anywhere in Africa or the diaspora.\nAwa
 rd: Micro-grants of USD 500 to USD 3\,000. Between 12 and 14 storytellers 
 will be selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Rolling. Applications sta
 y open until the end of the year or until 12 to 14 storytellers have been 
 selected\, whichever comes first\, so apply early rather than close to the
  nominal end date.\n\nMore: https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/communit
 y/kekere-storytellers-fund/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/community/kekere-storytellers-fun
 d/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Africans based anywhere in Africa or the diaspora.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pedantic-research-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T210037Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pedantic Research Grant (Pittsburgh): one to two week res
 earch stays
DESCRIPTION:The Pedantic Research Grant is a derivative program of the Peda
 ntic Arts Residency offering another way to be immersed in Pittsburgh's co
 mmunities: an independent opportunity for visual artists\, curators and wr
 iters to conduct self-motivated\, Pittsburgh-related research. The stay ru
 ns one or two weeks\, scheduled flexibly between the grantee and the Pedan
 tic Crew\, and is based on Penn Avenue in one of Pittsburgh's largest art 
 hubs. The grantee receives a free bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment\, an h
 onorarium of USD 500 or USD 1\,000 depending on length\, and help establis
 hing connections to individuals and organizations key to the research goal
 s. ELIGIBILITY: past Pedantic Arts Residency participants continuing to de
 velop their experiences\, or new candidates with a uniquely specific reaso
 n to be in Pittsburgh. APPLICATION: submit via the Open Call by 15 October
  for the upcoming cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Pedantic Arts\nLocation: Pittsbu
 rgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). For visual artists\,
  curators and writers with a specific reason to conduct Pittsburgh-related
  research\; also open to past Pedantic Arts Residency participants.\nAward
 : USD 500 (one week) or USD 1\,000 (two weeks) honorarium to use at the gr
 antee's discretion\, plus a free bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment and ass
 istance establishing connections relevant to the research goals. No applic
 ation fee mentioned.\nDuration: One or two weeks\, scheduled at the discre
 tion of the grantee and the Pedantic Crew.\n\nMore: https://pedanticarts.o
 rg/research-grant/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://pedanticarts.org/research-grant/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). For v
 isual artists\, curators and writers with a specific reason to conduct Pit
 tsburgh-related research\; also open to past Pedantic Arts Residency parti
 cipants.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
